{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>For You save</b> — the opposite of [what is] crooked." "<b>You save</b> — the opposite of תתפתל." "And he mentioned 'a people' — for it is a wonder to save a people, greater than the deliverance of a single man." "And he mentioned 'haughty eyes' — and they do not see at night."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:27:39.558349756Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}